// Christof_7_4_216            Milady Anezka. I must speak with thee.

// Anezka_7_4_217              Hush! Lest thou rouse the convent with thy clamor.
// Christof_7_4_218            I have wandered the city for hours, yet each turn of the streets did lead me back here.
// Anezka_7_4_219              My lord, 'tis dusk! Thou shouldst not be out of doors! Fiends shall soon be legion!
// Christof_7_4_220            I would fight all fiends of hell to stand at thy door.
// Anezka_7_4_221              And..and how may our holy order assist his lordship this eve?
// Christof_7_4_222            Milady, thou must hear me. I sought to tell thee once before, but fear took my voice.
// Anezka_7_4_223              What power could daunt the man who hath faced demons from hell?
// Christof_7_4_224            The face of an angel from heaven.
// Anezka_7_4_225              Oh. Milord, I…
// Christof_7_4_226            Thou hast stuck me a wound that heals not. My life's blood pours out before me and I cannot stanch it. I do love thee, fair Anezka! I do love thee with a passion I have never known!
