// Christof_7_4_228            If thou deny me I am undone!
// Anezka_7_4_229              I… I cannot deny thee. I too am afflicted with a wound for which thou art the only cure.
// Christof_7_4_230            Ah…
// Anezka_7_4_237              My soul fell when first I beheld thee. And now my heart is cleft in twain. My love of God and my love of thee have torn me to ribbons, for I must betray one to keep faith with the other.
// Christof_7_4_238            Thus my sins do pour out before me, for I have spilt my wickedness upon thy innocent bosom.
